- qjs-swallows-uncaught-exceptions-with-native-module: NOT a qjs-opencv
  bug - root cause lives in the `qjs` CLI / QuickJS engine itself (a
  separate project, not this repo), recorded here only because it was
  discovered while chasing an unrelated-looking "process exits silently"
  symptom. Confirmed the opencv module is not implicated:
  `import * as std from 'std'; gc();` (no opencv involved at all)
  reproduces the same silent exit(0) with no error printed, whereas the
  identical script with no import correctly prints the exception and
  exits 1. So this is a bug in how `qjs` reports uncaught top-level
  exceptions once *any* native module has been dynamically loaded via the
  module system - out of scope to fix from qjs-opencv. Worth reporting
  upstream / fixing in the quickjs project directly if it matters (it
  currently means any qjs-opencv script's uncaught errors are invisible).

    import * as std from 'std';
    console.log("before");
    gc(); // or any other uncaught exception
    console.log("after"); // never reached, and no error is printed either;
                           // process exits 0. Without the import, the
                           // same script prints the ReferenceError and
                           // exits 1 as expected.


- js-typedarray-type-biguint64array-parsed-as-signed: `js_typedarray_type()`
  (`include/js_typed_array.hpp`) detects an unsigned typed array by checking
  for a leading `'U'` character (`Uint8Array`, `Uint16Array`, ...), which
  misses `BigUint64Array` - its class name starts with `"Big"`, not `"U"`.
  `new Mat(new BigUint64Array([...]))` therefore silently builds a *signed*
  `CV_64S` Mat instead of `CV_64U`. Found while adding OpenCV 5.0's new
  integer depths (CV_64S/CV_64U/CV_32U/CV_Bool/CV_16BF) to this project's
  TypedArrayType <-> cv::Mat type mapping - `BigInt64Array` (signed) is
  unaffected and was the only one actually needed for LLM-inference input
  tensors (token ids), so this wasn't fixed inline. Same class of bug likely
  doesn't affect `Uint8Array`/`Uint16Array`/`Uint32Array` since those really
  do start with `'U'`.

    import { Mat, CV_64UC1 } from 'opencv';
    const m = new Mat(new BigUint64Array([1n, 2n]));
    console.log(m.type() === CV_64UC1); // false - actually CV_64S


- FIXED: opencv-js-api-mismatch-drawing-function-names: Renamed all
  drawing functions to match opencv.js API:
  - drawCircle → circle
  - drawLine → line
  - drawRect → rectangle
  - drawPolylines → polylines
  - drawPolygon → fillPoly (simplified to only call cv::fillPoly, removed thickness support)
  - drawEllipse → ellipse
  Changes made to js_draw.cpp (C++ exports and handler) and all 20+ client JS files.
  Note: drawContours and drawContour remain as-is (opencv.js has no direct equivalent).


- opencv-js-api-mismatch-contour-class: qjs-opencv provides a `Contour`
  class with convenience methods (approxPolyDP, arcLength, area, etc.)
  while opencv.js uses `MatVector` (of point-Mats) returned by
  `findContours`. All Contour methods must be replaced with free
  functions operating on Mat/MatVector, or Contour must become a
  compatibility shim over MatVector.
  Affected files:
    tests/test_video_homography.js
    tests/test_freetype.js
    tests/test_contours.js
    tests/test_grabcut.js
    contours.js
    js/cvVectorization.js
    ../doc-scanner.js
    ../scan.js
    ../test-umat.js
    ../test-cv.js
    ../test-quickjs.js
    ../test.js
    ../plot-cv.js
    ../test-diagram.js


- FIXED: opencv-js-api-mismatch-dnn-namespace: Five functions that exist
  in opencv.js (blobFromImage, readNet, readNetFromONNX,
  readNetFromTensorflow, readNetFromTFLite) are now exported at module
  level in addition to remaining in the dnn namespace for compatibility.
  Model wrapper classes (DetectionModel, ClassificationModel, etc.) and
  qjs-opencv-only functions (NMSBoxes, constants) remain under dnn.
  Affected files:
    examples/qwen25_inference.js        (added readNetFromONNX import)
    js/cvVectorization.js               (replaced dnn with flat imports)
    ../object_detection.js              (added readNet, blobFromImage)
    ../yolo.js                          (added blobFromImage)
    ../photo_categorizer.js             (added readNetFromONNX, blobFromImage)


- opencv-js-api-mismatch-line-class: qjs-opencv provides a `Line` class
  while opencv.js has no `Line` type — `HoughLinesP` returns a
  `PointVector` (vector<Vec4i> mapped to points). Code using `Line`
  must be reworked to use Point/Vec4i equivalents.
  Affected files:
    tests/test_fastlinedetector.js
    tests/test_linesegmentdetector.js
    tests/test_gif.js
    tests/fld_lines.js
    tests/test_video_writer.js
    ../diagram.js
    ../test-cv.js
    ../test-quickjs.js
    ../test-cli.js
    ../test-video.js
    ../test-opencv.js


- opencv-js-api-mismatch-draw-namespace: qjs-opencv provides a `Draw`
  namespace with methods like `Draw.line()`, `Draw.circle()`,
  `Draw.rectangle()`, `Draw.contours()`, `Draw.text()`, `Draw.textSize()`,
  `Draw.polylines()`, `Draw.loadFont()` while opencv.js has none of
  this — drawing is done via free functions (`line()`, `circle()`,
  `rectangle()`, `putText()`, etc.).
  Affected files:
    js/cvHighGUI.js
    ../test-umat.js
    ../test-diagram.js
    ../diagram.js
    ../test-cv.js
    ../test-quickjs.js
    ../test-cli.js
    ../test-video.js
    ../test-opencv.js


- opencv-js-api-mismatch-mat-accessors: qjs-opencv provides `mat.at(i,j)`
  (generic, type-inferred), `mat.set(i,j,v)`, and `mat.buffer`
  (raw ArrayBuffer). opencv.js provides type-specific accessors:
  `mat.ucharAt()`, `mat.intAt()`, `mat.floatAt()`, `mat.doubleAt()`,
  etc. (no generic `.at()`), and typed views `.data`, `.data32F`,
  `.data64F` (no `.buffer`). Also `mat.xor()`/`mat.and()` operator
  methods don't exist — opencv.js uses `cv.bitwise_xor()`/`cv.bitwise_and()`.
  Affected files:
    tests/test_worker.js               (mat.buffer — not flagged separately)
    examples/qwen25_inference.js       (mat.buffer, N-dim constructor)
    js/cvWorker.js                     (mat.buffer)
    js/vectorizer/cv/marshal.js        (mat.buffer)
    ../test-umat.js                    (mat.at, mat.set, mat.xor, mat.and, mat.buffer)
    ../test-cv.js                      (mat.at, mat.set)
    ../test-quickjs.js                 (mat.at, mat.set)


- opencv-js-api-mismatch-findcontours-signature: qjs-opencv's
  `findContours` can be called with 4 args (no hierarchy output param)
  while opencv.js requires 5 args: `findContours(image, contours,
  hierarchy, mode, method)` — hierarchy MatVector is mandatory.
  Affected files:
    ../doc-scanner.js
    ../scan.js


- NOT-A-BUG: opencv-js-api-mismatch-houghcircles-class: HoughCircles is
  already a plain free function in qjs-opencv (js_imgproc.cpp:2220),
  identical to opencv.js. No class/wrapper exists — the original BUGS
  entry was incorrect.


- opencv-js-api-mismatch-hu-moments-signature: qjs-opencv's
  `HuMoments(moments, outputArray)` takes 2 args (output-param style)
  while opencv.js has `cv.HuMoments(moments)` returning the result
  directly (1-arg, return-value style).
  Affected files:
    tests/test_contours.js
    ../test-video.js
    ../test-opencv.js


- opencv-js-api-mismatch-keypoint-constructor: qjs-opencv allows
  `new KeyPoint(point, size, ...)` while opencv.js's `KeyPoint` is a
  value_object with no JS constructor sugar — it's only returned by
  detector methods, not constructible.
  Affected files:
    tests/test_video_homography.js
    ../test-video.js
    ../test-opencv.js


- opencv-js-api-mismatch-barcode-detector-name: qjs-opencv exposes
  `BarcodeDetector` (short name) while opencv.js uses the full
  namespaced name `barcode_BarcodeDetector`.
  Affected files:
    tests/test_barcode.js


