- opencv-js-api-mismatch-feature2d-methods-vs-properties: qjs-opencv
  exposes `descriptorSize`, `descriptorType`, `defaultName` as
  properties while opencv.js has them as methods: `descriptorSize()`,
  `descriptorType()`, `getDefaultName()`. Also `Feature2D.write()`/
  `.read()` (serialize/deserialize) are absent from opencv.js.
  Affected files:
    ../test-features2d.js


- opencv-js-api-mismatch-cv64sc1-and-ndim-mat: `CV_64SC1` (OpenCV 5
  integer-depth addition) and N-dimensional Mat constructor
  `new Mat(dims, sizes[], type)` don't exist in opencv.js. opencv.js
  only has CV_8U through CV_64F depths and 2D constructors.
  Affected files:
    examples/qwen25_inference.js
